<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Single-pass Variant</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For completeness, we provide a variant that does not reorder <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and fuses
Pass-1 (dense intra-segment causal initialization) and Pass-2 (coordinate-scheduled prefix traversal with early stopping)
into a single streaming procedure.
Unlike the two-pass implementation that materializes intermediate online-softmax states <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A,Lbuf,Mbuf)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,Lbuf,Mbuf)</annotation></semantics></math> in (H)BM,
the fused variant keeps the per-query states <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,\ell,acc)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,\ell,acc)</annotation></semantics></math> in registers and updates them sequentially:
(i) it first scans intra-segment causal tiles to initialize the states (equivalent to Pass-1),
(ii) then computes a small dense local window for boundary stability,
and (iii) finally traverses historical prefix tiles in the retrieved order with a monotone-gain early-stopping rule.
See pseudocode in Alg. <a href="#alg4" title="Algorithm 4 ‣ C.3 Single-pass Variant ‣ Appendix C Additional Experimental Details ‣ S2O: Early Stopping for Sparse Attention via Online Permutation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg4" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 4</span> </span> Fused Pass-1+Pass-2 (Single-pass, No <math id="alg4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> Reordering): Coordinate-Scheduled Sparse Attention</figcaption>
<div id="alg4.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg4.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
